# ADR-0226, INV-0226-2: `date` shows the host's time (the RTC under QEMU
# follows the host), within 2 s of the host's clock at the moment the runner
# reads the line. A second reading after `sleep 3` is later than the first
# (the wall clock goes on with the monotonic one).
! panicked
! ZORAYA-FAULT
! no real-time clock reading
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
> date\r
D 2
< \r\n~>
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
> date\r
D 2
< \r\n~>
# ADR-0227, INV-0227-1: three programs of one boot get different bytes (the
# runner fails if two words after `random:` are equal, which "unavailable"
# would be).
! no entropy source
> random\r
< ok\r\n~>
> random\r
< ok\r\n~>
> random\r
< ok\r\n~>
U 3 random:
x power off
> poweroff\r
